
# 2026-08-04

Quiet, productive. Spent most of the morning on the Atlas first-run screen ([[Atlas Overview]]) and got the skeleton to a point where it can be shown without apologising for it. The trick was refusing to render anything at all until the vault knows whether it has content — the half-populated flash was doing more damage than the loading delay.

Short call with Tomas about Harbor ([[Harbor Overview]]) and its release cadence. He wants a freeze on Friday; I think Monday is more honest given where the migration sits. We left it unresolved, which is fine.

